  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Alterations including erection of front and rear dormer roof extensions to main roof  including raising the ridge by 400mm and erection of part single, part two-storey rear/side extension including enlargement of garage ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - By reason of the scale, design and siting of the proposed additions, the development would fail to maintain subservience to the existing property, would remove important character features and would appear unduly bulky, incongruous and harmful to its appearance. The proposed development would thereby cause harm to the character and appearance of the property, and 'less than substantial' harm to the character and appearance of the conservation area. There are not considered to be any public benefits to the proposal that would outweigh this identified harm. The proposed development is therefore considered to be unacceptable and contrary to policies LP1, LP3 or LP5 of the Local Plan (adopted July 2023), Section 72 (1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Policy HC1 (C) of the London Plan (2021) and paragraphs 212 or 215 of the NPPF (2024).",
    "Reason : 2 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to work with the applicant in a positive and proactive manner and the Council has, as far as practicable, sought solutions to problems arising in relation to dealing with the planning application. We have made available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan consisting of the Core Strategy, Development Management Policies Document, Supplementary Planning documents and where appropriate the Site Specific Allocations Document as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
